 routes=['<strong>EU citizens</strong> who plan to stay in Italy submit form AA4/8 to a local Agenzia office, with a valid passport or an identity card valid for travel abroad. They can also ask at the Italian consulate in their country.','<strong>Non-EU citizens arriving in Italy:</strong> the immigration desk (Sportello Unico per l’Immigrazione) in each Prefecture assigns the code to people applying for a permit for employment or family reunification, and the police headquarters (Questura) for other permits. The immigration desk first gives a numeric provisional code, and the definitive one comes with the residence permit. With the Questura the definitive code comes at once.','<strong>International protection:</strong> the Questura or the border police assigns the code when the application is submitted.','<strong>Unaccompanied or irregular minors:</strong> the Agenzia assigns the code on the request of the local health authority (ASL) that must enrol the minor.','<strong>Ukrainian refugees:</strong> the Questura issues the definitive code when the application for a temporary permit is filed.','<strong>Legally resident in Italy without a code:</strong> apply at any Agenzia office with a signed form AA4/8 and a valid identity document. The request must be justified.'],
 p1b=f'Foreign nationals who do not live in Italy can, according to the {a(M,"Italian Foreign Ministry pages")} (in Italian), delegate a person to file the request at an Agenzia office in Italy. Italian citizens registered abroad (AIRE) go through the consulate.',
 p2='The accepted documents are a valid residence permit; a valid passport with a visa where required, or another document recognised by the Italian authorities; a proof of identity issued by the diplomatic or consular representation in Italy of the country of origin; or an Italian identity card. The form and its instructions are on the Agenzia delle Entrate site.',
 p3='If the data of two or more people produce the same code, the immigration desk or the Questura invites the person to an Agenzia office, which issues the definitive code after a check. A provisional code is valid in the meantime. This is the case explained in the guide <a href="{{g:cos-e-l-omocodia}}">what is omocodia</a>.',
 p4='According to the brochure, the code is sent by ordinary mail to the address of residence for residents, or to the tax domicile given in the request for non-residents. Only the code issued and certified by the Agenzia delle Entrate is valid, and it does not expire. EU citizens use the Italian health service with the European Health Insurance Card of their country of residence.',
 p5=f'Use the spelling on your identity document. Only letters of the alphabet count: accents, apostrophes, spaces and hyphens are ignored, and an accented letter counts as the base letter. With several surnames, they are read from left to right as one surname, as {a("https://www.avvocatoandreani.it/servizi/calcolo_codice_fiscale.php","this description of the rule")} (in Italian) puts it. If your name is spelled differently on two documents, the official code can differ from the calculated one.',
